watch": "Fresh polling and the size of the Republican turnout operation in South Texas could tighten this into a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Vicente Gonzalez (D) is running."]}, "overview": "South Texas's 34th District is one of the closest House races on the map. Incumbent Vicente Gonzalez, a Democrat, faces Republican Eric Flores in a district that leans Republican by about three points, making this a genuine battleground despite Gonzalez's incumbency. Most expert raters call it Lean D, though Cook and Inside Elections rate it a Tossup, and prediction markets price the Democrat around 82-83%.\n\nGonzalez holds a clear financial edge, with $2.5 million on hand to Flores's $686,000, though Flores has raised nearly $2.9 million and drawn Republican outside support. The only recent independent poll, from August, showed Gonzalez up just three points. Republicans are investing heavily, with Vice President Vance headlining a rally in Harlingen in late September, underscoring how contested this seat remains.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7969, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7826, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7895, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8125, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7373, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7369, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7694, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7446, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8106, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7774, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7834, "margin": 4.5}]}